# public_eval_7491f3cf

The canonical rule parses the four framed panels, derives the largest
8-connected control object as a divider, and floods the singleton marker's
4-connected side.  It composes panel two inside that derived region and panel
three outside it into panel four.  Divider cells admit both sources, with the
marked-side source winning overlaps.

The native family adds the episode-fixed `source_assignment` parameter.  The
alternative swaps which source belongs to the marked region while preserving
all segmentation and composition mechanics.  Generated scenes vary frame and
role colors, panel dimensions, divider orientation, marker side, and source
textures; query streams are count-independent and include a 30-row case.

Owner registration, exact-source review, qualification, and acceptance are
still required.  This authoring source is not training-admitted.

Owner reference serialization correction: strict parsing exposed one extra closing parenthesis after each complete rule. Removed only that unconsumed character, preserving the parsed executable form. Original bytes and hashes are in evidence/strict-racket-serialization/repair.json; fresh protected execution and native acceptance determine current readiness.
